  'Spanish Phonetics and Pronunciation',
  'Spanish Phonetics and Pronunciation introduces the sound system of Spanish through articulatory phonetics, phonology, dialectal variation, transcription, and guided pronunciation practice. Students learn to describe Spanish sounds accurately, hear regional and learner differences, use IPA and recording tools, and design an individual improvement plan grounded in evidence rather than vague accent advice.',
  $sphojson${"slug": "spanish-phonetics-and-pronunciation", "title": "Spanish Phonetics and Pronunciation", "description": "Spanish Phonetics and Pronunciation introduces the sound system of Spanish through articulatory phonetics, phonology, dialectal variation, transcription, and guided pronunciation practice. Students learn to describe Spanish sounds accurately, hear regional and learner differences, use IPA and recording tools, and design an individual improvement plan grounded in evidence rather than vague accent advice.", "topics": [{"id": "a5f03d5d-6124-43c8-b89f-cfbabc891eb6", "type": "topic", "title": "Articulatory Phonetics and the Speech Mechanism", "description": "Students begin by learning how speech sounds are physically produced. This gives them a precise vocabulary for describing pronunciation instead of relying on imitation alone.", "children": [{"id": "c0464983-c686-49fa-ac3f-f75d1f0a48d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Speech organs and airflow", "children": [{"id": "7c6cc53c-95b9-46f1-b30f-ae309a214180", "type": "concept", "title": "Lungs and airflow"}, {"id": "a6e2d229-ecbe-4ff3-b29f-bd42bd03fe4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Vocal folds and voicing"}, {"id": "50b41021-475d-46ea-870f-e64dae8681af", "type": "concept", "title": "Tongue body, blade, and tip"}, {"id": "0f44c2f1-ca09-48d5-af0d-4cadf68572e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Lips, teeth, alveolar ridge, palate, and velum"}], "description": "Students connect pronunciation to breath, voicing, and the movement of articulators."}, {"id": "5ac0936f-4d90-4b6c-a1d0-0ee26f1f6b37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Place and manner of articulation", "children": [{"id": "a49fb67b-30b3-40f0-9f55-48b57899c5d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bilabial, dental, alveolar, palatal, velar"}, {"id": "fb58899e-0628-4e69-a9e6-470dbbfdb03a", "type": "concept", "title": "Stops, fricatives, approximants, nasals, laterals, rhotics"}, {"id": "b0b28796-769a-49f1-ae09-3a183624e897", "type": "concept", "title": "Voiced and voiceless contrasts"}, {"id": "79b8a98a-6c59-4980-870c-47ae5fdb18aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuants and obstruents"}], "description": "Students classify sounds by where and how they are made, which supports analysis, transcription, and feedback."}, {"id": "c70cb243-8399-4871-a6e0-09c5b6e3f342", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phonetics versus phonology", "children": [{"id": "f5f2782c-4d5b-4c92-bab1-341b8cb50bcc", "type": "concept", "title": "Phones and phonemes"}, {"id": "cc954205-5342-447b-9fb6-d553f86580e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Allophones"}, {"id": "621d9931-397c-423d-8195-aefc4bdd2cfd", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimal pairs"}, {"id": "c2d9c709-1273-46f7-83b1-af5699c5e056", "type": "concept", "title": "Broad versus narrow description"}], "description": "Students distinguish physical sound detail from the contrastive sound system of Spanish."}]}, {"id": "9c473e55-6e86-42b2-957a-1d6cca143ef4", "type": "topic", "title": "Spanish Vowels, Diphthongs, and Hiatus", "description": "Spanish vowel control is foundational because the five-vowel system carries stress, rhythm, clarity, and accent perception across varieties.", "children": [{"id": "8a2b69af-85c7-4bc6-9711-c26e8929f9dc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The five-vowel system", "children": [{"id": "3fea07ac-ab71-4d6b-813b-5f784c4175bb", "type": "concept", "title": "High, mid, and low vowels"}, {"id": "65c69123-c8bd-4ed5-b25e-fa4c4cb9fc89", "type": "concept", "title": "Front and back vowels"}, {"id": "75a12851-bd11-4ed1-8e15-db527594b18e", "type": "concept", "title": "Tense and steady vowel quality"}, {"id": "6f797aee-d5d0-4875-b87f-5e73c3d4d95a", "type": "concept", "title": "Unstressed vowel clarity"}], "description": "Students practice stable vowel quality and avoid reducing unstressed vowels as in English."}, {"id": "87edad10-2efc-441f-8918-ef6967a9eca8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diphthongs and glides", "children": [{"id": "b6512a4c-c946-414c-9346-b465c6213f2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Rising diphthongs"}, {"id": "9e77b2fb-42ac-4ed7-a297-8ac013b7363d", "type": "concept", "title": "Falling diphthongs"}, {"id": "f681a6b5-3395-4f66-a4ad-b4c419b57f7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Glides written i, y, and u"}, {"id": "d89fe077-5292-40df-b64a-843d9b700b62", "type": "concept", "title": "Common learner pronunciation traps"}], "description": "Students learn how vowel sequences form one syllable or two and how that affects stress and spelling."}, {"id": "1023f18e-a2e4-48c6-8493-e5fbbf03d541", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hiatus and accent marks", "children": [{"id": "4e42d1e9-9248-47b3-bedf-1fbe5763c246", "type": "concept", "title": "Hiatus versus diphthong"}, {"id": "7142d130-f26a-464c-a0ea-480063612bd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Stressed weak vowels"}, {"id": "f8c6b33d-88e1-4614-bc83-fadf4901a514", "type": "concept", "title": "Written accents to mark hiatus"}, {"id": "4a5597cd-5a0d-4ad6-9f3c-01cb12be61ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Practice with pairs such as hacia and hacia-like contrasts"}], "description": "Students connect sound structure to written accentuation and oral rhythm."}]}, {"id": "a676f87e-7317-4685-9a8b-ecf9b1e1f618", "type": "topic", "title": "Consonant System and Sound-Spelling Correspondence", "description": "This unit links Spanish orthography to pronunciation while making clear that letters and sounds are not the same object.", "children": [{"id": "c64b840c-d0c9-4a6a-8b43-34cd94d7401c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consonant inventory", "children": [{"id": "9e264e69-3ff7-4a1f-b799-0406817826e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Stops and approximants"}, {"id": "4a97d936-5f52-4d2b-a2c1-fd75facb6ef4", "type": "concept", "title": "Nasals"}, {"id": "11ba4d2b-6aef-461c-a2a9-aba5a1092777", "type": "concept", "title": "Fricatives and affricates"}, {"id": "0e31719a-a16b-4cfe-b40a-5e8e770511e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Laterals and rhotics"}], "description": "Students learn the main consonant categories and where they contrast in Spanish."}, {"id": "5af15ebd-2e06-4e79-a92d-7b202818fb15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grapheme-to-sound patterns", "children": [{"id": "4e0ab87d-608f-4496-8d81-1fb032d951e2", "type": "concept", "title": "c, z, s patterns"}, {"id": "8c307476-5e73-48d4-b24d-d0b2470e75a7", "type": "concept", "title": "g, j, gu, and gue/gui"}, {"id": "51469690-a9cc-4149-9c5e-31402360ffc5", "type": "concept", "title": "ll, y, h, x"}, {"id": "55a9aba7-403a-4d8d-a59a-8da2890b6c8e", "type": "concept", "title": "b and v as one phonological category in most Spanish"}], "description": "Students practice reliable spelling-to-sound rules and the exceptions that matter most."}, {"id": "64c8dfae-8841-4774-b7e2-94fce375a6e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Learner transfer issues", "children": [{"id": "989a40ee-81db-436a-981d-de2eaa03705d", "type": "concept", "title": "Aspirated p, t, k"}, {"id": "b3cc0f74-24e2-4734-a14d-517fd4c1e274", "type": "concept", "title": "English-like v"}, {"id": "8075240e-0ad0-41e0-81cc-1173638cbbbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Schwa insertion"}, {"id": "c01e1c07-1021-4137-a5bf-7ea38f2a805a", "type": "concept", "title": "Over-pronouncing h or final consonants"}], "description": "Students identify English-influenced habits that reduce intelligibility or naturalness."}]}, {"id": "f942119a-bfcd-4442-95b9-c528a96ee2db", "type": "topic", "title": "Stops, Approximants, and Spirantization", "description": "Students learn one of the most important patterns for natural Spanish pronunciation: voiced stops often become approximant-like between vowels and in other non-fortifying contexts.", "children": [{"id": "b6319eec-5264-4d38-9069-e8793de9d5e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voiceless stops", "children": [{"id": "2c2097e2-e11e-4e09-8cbb-70f825dce70e", "type": "concept", "title": "Unaspirated release"}, {"id": "f0f94509-f39e-4fa9-a779-f6e6a6011ede", "type": "concept", "title": "Dental t"}, {"id": "9d6e8481-4f17-429b-a6c7-4b4f0c7c7a53", "type": "concept", "title": "Word-initial position"}, {"id": "fe456b1e-bb46-47ad-80b1-01588a57934e", "type": "concept", "title": "Clusters with r and l"}], "description": "Students build accurate timing and articulation for p, t, and k without English-style aspiration."}, {"id": "9df92a8a-8dda-4239-bb34-e31573147599", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voiced stop alternations", "children": [{"id": "2dedada4-da8d-4a21-a0ed-34516c870bdf", "type": "concept", "title": "After pause"}, {"id": "8d6c1775-bce1-4d72-9429-4fb5386fb45e", "type": "concept", "title": "After nasal consonants"}, {"id": "6362ffe8-6f06-461f-a308-f40511c8946c", "type": "concept", "title": "After lateral for d"}, {"id": "660663ff-75d9-412a-8e46-0517c60420aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Intervocalic and phrase-internal contexts"}], "description": "Students learn when b, d, and g sound stop-like and when they become softer continuants."}, {"id": "cbc2f154-162d-489e-adcb-52147cd16fa6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Connected-speech practice", "children": [{"id": "975404c0-fab4-4627-b44f-66d95e0010b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Phrase boundaries"}, {"id": "a50d6a98-d073-418b-8075-768af5d5ea5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Fast versus careful speech"}, {"id": "037d4d15-dddf-48d7-a08f-908a21e1d7d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimal phrase drills"}, {"id": "42d17e76-ae6c-4006-9955-0ec95314c956", "type": "concept", "title": "Recording and self-assessment"}], "description": "Students apply spirantization in phrases rather than isolated word lists."}]}, {"id": "04270785-3829-43cc-9f36-54fd9ac0936a", "type": "topic", "title": "Rhotics, Laterals, and High-Difficulty Consonants", "description": "The tap, trill, and lateral system often separates intelligible pronunciation from highly polished pronunciation, so this unit combines phonetic analysis with motor practice.", "children": [{"id": "5dbb1100-f07b-4b9f-b1d6-e020cb844528", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tap and trill contrast", "children": [{"id": "07c6efa3-6a78-413e-b499-171da02f79cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Intervocalic contrast"}, {"id": "28d3ca0a-8acd-4b00-9b2f-1fa50b69d0cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Word-initial trill"}, {"id": "26f880dc-59d3-4b20-b166-38f991c423fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Trill after n, l, and s"}, {"id": "97bbd5b2-6e92-4f7a-a17c-e6a6f667c8e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Tap in clusters"}], "description": "Students learn distribution, contrast, and production strategies for the two Spanish r sounds."}, {"id": "e1362014-93d1-4c7a-b1a1-2351e2304034", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Laterals and palatal contrasts", "children": [{"id": "f9a6ba17-f126-42c5-a25f-d2c7143236d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear Spanish l"}, {"id": "1e19cab7-fd87-4461-a756-392409444db0", "type": "concept", "title": "ll/y merger awareness"}, {"id": "6982d8e9-2761-47d3-becb-3ccac81ea92f", "type": "concept", "title": "Yeismo"}, {"id": "f36178dd-0b75-4cbb-9d1b-be3bd9b269bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Regional palatal realizations"}], "description": "Students connect l, ll, and y patterns to pronunciation and dialect."}, {"id": "0cf21a65-a773-429c-a930-7bd77babbdf9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Practice methods", "children": [{"id": "ef65beb6-531c-4ee0-824f-e723769058a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Motor warmups"}, {"id": "a907f828-0db2-4f9a-b6d1-1fade2753e6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Syllable ladders"}, {"id": "cef89248-8648-4865-ab68-dcbed6d4bc0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimal and near-minimal pairs"}, {"id": "86531cb5-8681-4007-9e5f-fb49f1524d28", "type": "concept", "title": "Recorded progress checks"}], "description": "Students use targeted drills without reducing pronunciation to mechanical repetition."}]}, {"id": "c0dee42e-7e2c-4495-9936-f9134cb50945", "type": "topic", "title": "Syllabification, Stress, and Accentuation", "description": "This unit ties sound, spelling, and rhythm together. Students learn to predict stress, divide syllables, and explain accent marks.", "children": [{"id": "e847d224-9fb6-4729-a9df-13c2c13a97cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Syllable structure", "children": [{"id": "da11944b-bb6c-4b84-bebe-714a92d062e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Open and closed syllables"}, {"id": "7b670da4-cfa3-472a-bb3a-9caa1f3dd48a", "type": "concept", "title": "Onset clusters"}, {"id": "647abbfb-8283-4d6d-861e-c6592ddc9f21", "type": "concept", "title": "Coda consonants"}, {"id": "365c0647-f33f-4a26-85c8-eb1ac2323506", "type": "concept", "title": "Syllable boundaries across words"}], "description": "Students identify onsets, nuclei, codas, and clusters in Spanish words."}, {"id": "42754728-2e24-49a7-9795-07500cd884b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lexical stress rules", "children": [{"id": "87ec58f5-8324-470b-b90d-de4ceab8fbb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Words ending in vowel, n, or s"}, {"id": "c514d79c-73f7-4194-a3f7-afc251077b34", "type": "concept", "title": "Words ending in other consonants"}, {"id": "29ea7e78-b199-494d-8325-3a805eacb64f", "type": "concept", "title": "Antepenultimate stress"}, {"id": "e5c5fb75-4353-43f4-9710-8f879bbb1d83", "type": "concept", "title": "Stress-only minimal pairs"}], "description": "Students learn regular stress patterns and when written accents override them."}, {"id": "82cdcae4-2d00-4263-9855-37c682752ec9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accentuation and pronunciation", "children": [{"id": "7d0b48d1-0711-4b55-86fe-7a37b3671861", "type": "concept", "title": "Diacritical accents"}, {"id": "e7272a73-cdf1-459e-83cf-d28b49f992e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Question words"}, {"id": "e98bf9cf-c8a3-46d6-b3dc-61ff61a032f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Hiatus marking"}, {"id": "effcb3cc-4748-4fea-a6a7-439f478b583e", "type": "concept", "title": "Proofreading for accent errors"}], "description": "Students connect written accents to pronunciation, grammar, and meaning."}]}, {"id": "144148cc-840e-4fc2-abe1-a4e16439a027", "type": "topic", "title": "Intonation, Rhythm, and Prosody", "description": "Pronunciation is more than individual sounds. This unit helps students hear and produce Spanish rhythm, phrasing, pitch movement, and emphasis.", "children": [{"id": "b73a5b66-eaa1-48d3-9070-ae57f14925e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rhythm and timing", "children": [{"id": "0221e46a-a036-4880-803d-c2184d8aaa83", "type": "concept", "title": "Syllable prominence"}, {"id": "053b1bb2-9036-43e8-b072-19f04e27ff43", "type": "concept", "title": "Vowel clarity in unstressed syllables"}, {"id": "fc18c7cb-b2e9-4fa2-98c3-92065ec42be7", "type": "concept", "title": "Phrase grouping"}, {"id": "9741ca84-85f7-494b-8018-84930ca70aa2", "type": "concept", "title": "Tempo control"}], "description": "Students explore how Spanish rhythm differs from English-influenced timing."}, {"id": "19a2eb28-cfb9-42be-ad3e-df4c3bdc640a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intonation contours", "children": [{"id": "1e13184c-49c2-4a8e-952a-7618a6dba2b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Declaratives"}, {"id": "68589a3f-59d2-4d7c-83a0-92f270dba8b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Yes/no questions"}, {"id": "765a33b5-e5eb-4848-a8e5-e148f39da83a", "type": "concept", "title": "Information questions"}, {"id": "93918776-b32c-41a1-8646-2e5441e6f70c", "type": "concept", "title": "Enumerations and parentheticals"}], "description": "Students practice pitch movement in statements, questions, lists, and emphasis."}, {"id": "0322ab1a-00a1-4e2a-b5ef-35dd2d00abee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prosody and meaning", "children": [{"id": "aaa00d1c-6b53-4209-a7c1-cb85e013298f", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrastive emphasis"}, {"id": "eb71facc-e6b3-44d0-a960-5cbf312af973", "type": "concept", "title": "Turn-taking"}, {"id": "07026a15-094c-4196-a154-379fad80dad9", "type": "concept", "title": "Politeness and requests"}, {"id": "8047dc49-7f00-4b62-8bfc-6c2f26e15cf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Reading aloud with interpretation"}], "description": "Students connect intonation to stance, politeness, focus, and discourse management."}]}, {"id": "7f231e3a-3fb1-4931-b791-c3741c742271", "type": "topic", "title": "Dialectal and Sociophonetic Variation", "description": "World-class pronunciation study treats variation as normal, systematic, and culturally meaningful. Students learn to recognize major patterns without ranking varieties.", "children": [{"id": "82dc5176-7f9e-4504-9d0c-e9cd3176f60a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major regional patterns", "children": [{"id": "7df3cdf4-344e-468c-8310-2bbbdb402e19", "type": "concept", "title": "Seseo, distincion, and ceceo"}, {"id": "a7ee7b46-81af-44b3-9135-beae7b9f58e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Yeismo and regional y/ll realizations"}, {"id": "30038e38-ce41-4be2-8dab-c5fefc236dbc", "type": "concept", "title": "Final s weakening"}, {"id": "e7bd4501-5279-411d-91ad-eb8b7970dfe1", "type": "concept", "title": "Caribbean, Andean, Mexican, Rioplatense, and Peninsular patterns"}], "description": "Students identify common pronunciation differences across Spain, Latin America, the Caribbean, and U.S. Spanish."}, {"id": "2396f215-c51c-4ae4-9657-3f42629d4909", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social and stylistic variation", "children": [{"id": "66acc653-a3a7-4ff6-8de9-fb537fb24841", "type": "concept", "title": "Careful versus casual speech"}, {"id": "37ae4461-1a4c-434e-928d-ca8e1c3e2410", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban and rural patterns"}, {"id": "fdb43565-dcc7-4e83-b691-f448fcab7e9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Age and community patterns"}, {"id": "c17bcb1f-1a30-4952-b833-fee89d60be26", "type": "concept", "title": "Register and performance"}], "description": "Students study how pronunciation shifts by setting, identity, formality, and speech rate."}, {"id": "6f596ca7-ed70-4cce-88c5-db2ceea60050", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Listening across varieties", "children": [{"id": "545818ee-3eb0-43c5-a6b0-8ab409265422", "type": "concept", "title": "Accent mapping"}, {"id": "bbe6488c-2729-4cdd-a491-dfdf833fdd20", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative listening logs"}, {"id": "c07a0ae1-c2e8-4f66-8284-fff0d4cbc42c", "type": "concept", "title": "Transcription of regional samples"}, {"id": "36e17445-edfe-4bc9-afdd-8ec0e39d1453", "type": "concept", "title": "Respectful description of variation"}], "description": "Students build comprehension strategies for real-world Spanish rather than one classroom accent."}]}, {"id": "3a1c04fa-fc3d-45ff-813f-de6d3837b95b", "type": "topic", "title": "IPA and Phonetic Transcription", "description": "Transcription gives students a disciplined way to hear details, document pronunciation, and compare varieties.", "children": [{"id": "f5e25ef4-08ea-4dc0-9f1d-6b8e81c98b6f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IPA fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "fe055b1c-8a9b-4376-bac3-d8f70e3fff34", "type": "concept", "title": "Consonant chart orientation"}, {"id": "50393c0b-e93d-4546-bdc9-90f453f9e101", "type": "concept", "title": "Vowel chart orientation"}, {"id": "5b81ac75-2f85-491e-9605-282220b8a8ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Suprasegmental marks"}, {"id": "a154a28f-8e3f-479d-beea-00f07f6f9b64", "type": "concept", "title": "Diacritics for careful description"}], "description": "Students learn to use the International Phonetic Alphabet for Spanish sounds without overloading the course with irrelevant symbols."}, {"id": "a98deb49-a845-4341-a877-04ab9c1cb15e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Broad transcription", "children": [{"id": "04895e14-5d70-4261-a3ff-659db5cfc62d", "type": "concept", "title": "Slash notation"}, {"id": "7cc8575d-3af5-4afc-a7bf-a0e515d030a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Phoneme inventory"}, {"id": "82b4d089-b0b5-41ff-8720-0dcb3b1b77c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Stress marking"}, {"id": "98d51b25-55bc-48d2-9cc4-8847053aaef1", "type": "concept", "title": "Syllable boundaries when useful"}], "description": "Students represent phonemic contrasts and predictable stress clearly."}, {"id": "9455ab45-ab9d-46be-ab1a-03c3ef6d0c2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Narrow transcription", "children": [{"id": "1c03cec5-d5b3-4716-82aa-759dda0efe93", "type": "concept", "title": "Allophones"}, {"id": "a3e1c504-00da-4033-8ce5-f49d22042e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Spirantization"}, {"id": "9774d705-24a1-4d14-9f8a-f656d9a0c62e", "type": "concept", "title": "Assimilation"}, {"id": "ab0a6f9e-a015-49af-ae86-5ed2e2251efa", "type": "concept", "title": "Regional realizations"}], "description": "Students add phonetic detail when it matters for pronunciation diagnosis or dialect comparison."}]}, {"id": "8794f592-1953-4ec4-9155-2ff64ef58c4d", "type": "topic", "title": "Acoustic Analysis and Technology-Assisted Feedback", "description": "Modern pronunciation courses benefit from visual and audio evidence. Students learn to use recordings, waveforms, and spectrograms as feedback tools.", "children": [{"id": "70de9282-f2c3-4ea5-a876-3d9c29b4b8fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recording methods", "children": [{"id": "91c0ee30-4098-4d68-8f1a-e9f90288686c", "type": "concept", "title": "Microphone placement"}, {"id": "8dc71e3a-7228-4591-ab84-8706199c4329", "type": "concept", "title": "Quiet recording environment"}, {"id": "4dc96620-adf3-45ea-b2d5-37fb684a24ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistent reading passages"}, {"id": "fcca400b-261b-450d-b8e5-22e13d879c8a", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming and storage"}], "description": "Students collect usable audio for analysis and progress tracking."}, {"id": "fe8b7de1-a950-4b76-ae3a-c5f04de35a5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Basic acoustic cues", "children": [{"id": "15bbdc8a-b355-4b44-9d8f-5037edadbd97", "type": "concept", "title": "Waveforms"}, {"id": "741ae9a3-8727-4587-89f1-206f0d583597", "type": "concept", "title": "Spectrograms"}, {"id": "294471d7-3af5-4c64-ac5a-0fa7e3ba78d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice onset time"}, {"id": "9ee84a3e-e06f-4170-adf9-3666215359a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Duration, pitch, and intensity"}], "description": "Students learn what visual displays can and cannot tell them about speech."}, {"id": "2f9f78ed-c2e1-4a95-a373-61d2952828cc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feedback workflow", "children": [{"id": "3f518896-e484-433c-80f4-5f392848dadc", "type": "concept", "title": "Compare model and self-recording"}, {"id": "6e901a31-47ab-42fe-ab20-9f83aaaff6ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Identify one feature at a time"}, {"id": "2508ab6e-0d34-44f9-b191-6ef56cf6966c", "type": "concept", "title": "Practice plan"}, {"id": "69ba80d1-0c35-4acb-a17e-022695096a6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflective progress notes"}], "description": "Students turn analysis into targeted pronunciation goals."}]}, {"id": "11989127-2702-4554-af5b-573c268af5c8", "type": "topic", "title": "Pronunciation Diagnostics and Individual Improvement Plan", "description": "Students learn to diagnose their own pronunciation profile and set priorities based on intelligibility, communicative goals, and measurable progress.", "children": [{"id": "13c80681-6653-430c-8768-7464394ad6f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnostic assessment", "children": [{"id": "4523bbee-c7b3-4b3c-804a-cb255a9559ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Read-aloud passage"}, {"id": "cd0cc2b5-c9e3-4cfd-86d1-65191700dd7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Picture narration"}, {"id": "f1804693-3a1a-4036-8a28-3a57e4b1d5b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Conversation sample"}, {"id": "0736fb20-e0fb-429d-b913-0316e42acdf2", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimal-pair perception check"}], "description": "Students gather evidence from reading, spontaneous speech, and listening tasks."}, {"id": "764a8bab-26ae-4837-a2f9-c63c7d2b6e70", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Error analysis", "children": [{"id": "93bf9b31-3fe4-44fe-a651-6a4908d04d43", "type": "concept", "title": "Segmental patterns"}, {"id": "47abb2f5-45d9-45af-802e-7609258a6531", "type": "concept", "title": "Stress and rhythm patterns"}, {"id": "a89d96d2-cd6c-4b98-be0a-05bbbeab048f", "type": "concept", "title": "Transfer from English or another language"}, {"id": "0630780e-702c-469d-a84d-9551b3ea3890", "type": "concept", "title": "Dialect versus learner error"}], "description": "Students distinguish occasional slips from systematic patterns."}, {"id": "41a725d8-72ff-42e0-b081-0c18356ea1c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Improvement plan", "children": [{"id": "c211c301-d787-4278-a600-a1446cf2bd1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Priority ranking"}, {"id": "ffed737c-5fa7-4dc1-ba56-7df01b93e372", "type": "concept", "title": "Daily practice routine"}, {"id": "96021034-5d7a-499d-94d4-7053940caa7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer and instructor feedback"}, {"id": "7b5dbfa0-e63b-49c1-8a1d-8aa1d053f802", "type": "concept", "title": "Midterm and final comparison"}], "description": "Students choose realistic goals and document strategies."}]}, {"id": "136439de-5f62-46b4-955d-a1cdb909ba23", "type": "topic", "title": "Recorded Speech Project and Oral Performance", "description": "The final project integrates the course: students analyze pronunciation, revise delivery, and present a polished spoken artifact with a reflection on evidence-based improvement.", "children": [{"id": "fe8d91fc-0724-48f1-9728-c1a31a41e8e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project design", "children": [{"id": "fbf167f4-b873-45ba-b8ee-60260862422a", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative, interview, poem, or presentation"}, {"id": "dce2d623-6100-4b58-bdc1-fc6dad2aa7b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Target accent or variety statement"}, {"id": "c7e16955-fc96-48b7-b043-d18c8b66dc55", "type": "concept", "title": "Script and spontaneous component"}, {"id": "4bebe97e-0573-49e4-8c8b-4fc6fc05e0a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical use of recordings"}], "description": "Students choose a speech sample that is meaningful, challenging, and appropriate for analysis."}, {"id": "22a5b18b-a80c-44ea-9549-fb2d7f76df40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revision and rehearsal", "children": [{"id": "e9bcffe4-0ce3-46a2-b798-eb601612092d", "type": "concept", "title": "Segmental focus"}, {"id": "0e594e84-7101-48ec-9b9e-87b98ad476dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Prosodic focus"}, {"id": "ca15359a-44ee-4473-a57e-1efc71c4af60", "type": "concept", "title": "Fluency and pacing"}, {"id": "51cb5f1c-1d33-43f2-9063-2325b0542845", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience awareness"}], "description": "Students use course tools to improve delivery without erasing their own voice."}, {"id": "45d4baf8-c266-4ab2-bf4c-11904b1211f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final analysis and reflection", "children": [{"id": "6bab28bb-627b-46f6-96ae-05902e8eb203", "type": "concept", "title": "Before-and-after comparison"}, {"id": "9e3de3c5-f14b-40e4-90d3-c9e3d7b96230", "type": "concept", "title": "Transcription excerpt"}, {"id": "d14a83b8-4efc-463c-b864-a6828c0ae03d", "type": "concept", "title": "Acoustic or auditory evidence"}, {"id": "9ca6885c-49af-4331-924e-c6ae94ab0199", "type": "concept", "title": "Final reflection memo"}], "description": "Students explain what changed, what evidence supports the change, and what remains a long-term goal."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$sphojson$::jsonb,
